WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.860
Could there be a real contest at the Democratic
convention for the nomination?

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.280
Very unlikely.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:17.349
The way the Democratic rules work, Hillary
Clinton is almost certain to get enough delegates

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:18.599
to win the nomination.

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:23.250
But there could be fireworks, or at least
intrigue, at that Democratic convention in

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.919
Philadelphia because Sanders is going to come
in with 40% or more of the delegates and a

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:35.050
strong and ardent base that doesn’t start
out with enthusiasm for the Democratic nominee.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.210
So Bernie Sanders might ask to change the
platform

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.679
to promote a single payer health care system

00:00:41.679 --> 00:00:44.539
to promote a return to Glass-Steagall

00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:47.929
and a strong pledge to breakup the big banks.

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:54.239
He could make a strong pitch to take on the
trade issue in a tougher way than the platform

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:56.050
would normally do.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:01.449
Or Sanders could ask for a choice of running
mate that might include an Elizabeth Warren

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:07.280
or a Sherrod Brown or somebody else who has
the same kind of ardent populist views that Sanders

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:07.780
does.

